    "imageonly":true,
    "defination" :[
      {
        "title":"",
        "phase": '<p class="dmn"><b>Domain 8: Hematologic Malignancies, General Considerations: Diagnostic Tests, Cytogenetics and Molecular Markers</b></p><table class="table"><tr><td class="th"><p class="T2"><b>B-ALL</b></p></td><td class="th"><p class="T2"><b>T-Cell ALL (T-ALL)</b></p></td><td class="th"><p class="T2"><b>Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p class="td_p">&#160;</p><p class="td_p">&#160;</p><p class="td_p"><b>Favorable Prognosis</b></p><p class="td_p">ETV6-RUNX1 t(12;21)(p13.2;q22.1)</p><p class="td_p">Trisomy 4 and 10</p><p class="td_p"><b>Poor Prognosis</b></p><p class="td_p">BCR-ABL1 t(9;22)(q34.1;q11.2)</p><p class="td_p">KMT2A (MLL) translocation</p><p class="td_p">iAMP21</p><p class="td_p">PAX5</p><p class="td_p">JAK1</p><p class="td_p">JAK2</p><p class="td_p">IKZF1</p><p class="td_p">CRLF2</p></td><td><p class="td_p">NOTCH1</p><p class="td_p">LMO1/2</p><p class="td_p">FBXW7</p><p class="td_p">SPI1-fusions</p></td><td><p class="td_p">&#160;</p><p class="td_p">&#160;</p><p class="td_p"><b>Favorable Prognosis</b></p><p class="td_p">NPM1</p><p class="td_p">CEBPA</p><p class="td_p"><b>Poor Prognosis</b></p><p class="td_p">FLT3-ITD</p><p class="td_p">IDH1</p><p class="td_p">IDH2</p><p class="td_p">TET2</p><p class="td_p">WT1</p><p class="td_p">DNMT3A</p><p class="td_p">TP53</p><p class="td_p">RUNX1</p></td></tr></table><div class="key"><p><b>Key Point:</b> Identify relevant molecular abnormalities for acute leukemia.</p></div><div class="suggested_readings"><p><u>Suggested Readings</u></p><p>de Haas V, Ismaila N, Advani A, et al. Initial diagnostic work-up of acute leukemia: ASCO clinical practice guideline endorsement of the college of American Pathologists and American Society of hematology guideline. <i>J Clin Oncol</i>. 2019;37(3):239-253. doi:<a href="https://doi.org/10.1200/JCO.18.01468">10.1200/JCO.18.01468</a></p><p>P&#x00F6;l&#x00F6;nen P, Mullighan CG, Teachey DT. Classification and risk stratification in T-lineage acute lymphoblastic leukemia. <i>Blood</i>. 2025;145(14):1464-1474. doi:<a href="https://doi.org/10.1182/blood.2023022920">10.1182/blood&#8203;.2023022920</a></p></div>'
      }
    ]
