    "term":'<p class="qz-txt"><b>A 6-month-old infant was diagnosed with B-ALL with a KMT2A rearrangement. The patient initially achieved remission on standard induction therapy but relapsed 6 months later with new-onset fever, pancytopenia, and circulating blasts. Repeat flow cytometry now reveals&#x00A0;expression of myeloid markers.</b></p><div class="key1"><p><b>What should the provider consider as a possible explanation for this clinical scenario, and what diagnostic steps should be taken?</b></p></div>',
    "termaudio":"",
